<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Pact</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as National Pact (Lebanon)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Pact is an unwritten agreement made in 1943 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>'s first president, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bechara-el-khoury">Bechara El Khoury</a>, a Maronite, and prime minister, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riad-al-solh">Riad Al Solh</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> Muslim. Christians agreed not to seek Western protection and Muslims not to seek union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, and the main offices were shared among religious communities. It laid the foundation of Lebanon's confessional system of government.</p></div>
